  "_MerchantAuth_note": "Merchant-user BFF OIDC client (REQ-8/9/14). The section is 'MerchantAuth' with a Providers map keyed by provider name — multi-provider-oidc renamed it away from the old single-client 'MerchantUser:Oidc' shape, which nothing reads anymore. Leave ClientId blank to keep merchant-user login disabled locally (the scheme is skipped); set both to a real 'Web application' Google client to exercise the live flow. Its registered redirect_uri must be <origin the browser actually hits>/api/v1/merchants/auth/google/callback — the SPA proxy origin, not the API port, whenever the SPA proxies /api. RegisterUrl is deliberately left at its relative default ('/register', made absolute against MerchantUser:Session:SpaBaseUrl at redirect time): a committed absolute localhost value is how a localhost redirect ships to production.",
  "MerchantAuth": {
    "Providers": {
      "Google": {
        "ClientId": "",
        "ClientSecret": ""
      }
    }
  },
  "Cors": {
    "_note": "Two dev SPA origins, two distinct CORS policies (BuildingBlocks.Web/CorsExtensions.cs): AllowedOrigins = merchant-user console :5300 (default policy); AdminOrigins = admin console :5200 (/api/v1/admins/* only). These are the origins the browser actually hits — each console proxies /api to the API on :5100, so a Google client's redirect URI is registered against the console port, never 5100.",
    "AllowedOrigins": ["http://localhost:5300"],
    "AdminOrigins": ["http://localhost:5200"]
  },
